You are a senior AI/ML engineer working on ATLAS — an internal RAG system 
at Comcast that answers questions from Confluence knowledge bases. 
ATLAS currently achieves 92% accuracy on a 50-question benchmark.

Your task is to implement OKF (Organized Knowledge Format) preprocessing 
layer that works alongside the existing GraphRAG system to push accuracy 
above 94%.

## ATLAS Current Stack
- Python 3.12 + FastAPI
- Azure OpenAI (GPT-4o + GPT-4o-mini + text-embedding-3-large)
- PostgreSQL + pgvector (vector store)
- Elasticsearch (BM25 keyword search)
- Redis (caching)
- Confluence (knowledge source — 4,800+ chunks, 6 spaces)

## Existing ATLAS Architecture (DO NOT BREAK THESE)

### Current Retrieval Pipeline
1. Hybrid search: 30% BM25 keyword + 50% vector similarity
2. Multi-signal reranking:
   - severity_weight, rarity_bonus, temporal_proximity, first_occurrence_bonus
   - page_type scoring: howto/reference +0.05, report -0.25
   - label scoring: deprecated -0.15, official +0.05
3. HIGH confidence threshold: avg >= 0.75 AND spread < 0.15
4. Multi-hop: BM25 second pass when top score < 0.60
5. CamelCase BM25 tokenizer splitting
6. Max 5 sources returned

### Current GraphRAG (PRESERVE THIS)
Each chunk has metadata:
{
  "ancestor_titles": ["Parent Page", "Section", "Grandparent"],
  "space": "PAYMENTS",
  "page_type": "howto",
  "labels": ["official", "active"],
  "source_url": "https://confluence.comcast.com/...",
  "title": "Page Title"
}

### Current Chunk Schema in pgvector
- id, content, embedding, source_url, title, space
- page_type, labels, ancestor_titles, score

## What You Need to Build

### 1. OKF Converter (okf_converter.py)

Build a class OKFConverter that:
- Takes raw Confluence page content + metadata as input
- Calls Azure OpenAI GPT-4o-mini to convert it to structured Markdown
- Uses this EXACT OKF schema:

---
# [Concept Name]

## Summary
One paragraph plain English explanation.

## Key Facts
- Fact 1
- Fact 2

## How It Works
Step by step explanation.

## Common Issues / FAQs
**Q: How do I...?**
A: ...

## Related Concepts
- [[ConceptA]]
- [[ConceptB]]

## Metadata
- Source: [Confluence URL]
- Space: [Space Key]  
- Page Type: howto / reference / policy / report
- Last Updated: [date]
- Status: active / deprecated
---

Requirements:
- Batch process with rate limiting (max 10 concurrent Azure OpenAI calls)
- Retry logic with exponential backoff (3 retries)
- Save OKF files to okf_knowledge_base/ directory locally
- Track conversion cost per page (input/output tokens)
- Skip pages already converted (check okf_knowledge_base/ for existing file)
- Log conversion progress with page title and status
- Handle errors gracefully — failed pages go to failed_conversions.json

The system prompt for conversion must:
- Instruct GPT-4o-mini to output ONLY Markdown, no preamble
- Tell it to extract [[RelatedConcept]] links from any hyperlinks, 
  "see also" sections, or mentions of other services/concepts in the page
- Tell it to mark deprecated if labels contain "deprecated" or 
  content mentions "deprecated", "legacy", "do not use"
- Tell it to skip navigation elements, breadcrumbs, formatting artifacts
- Temperature: 0 (deterministic output)

### 2. OKF-Aware Chunker (okf_chunker.py)

Build OKFAwareChunker that:
- Chunks by Markdown ## sections (not fixed token windows)
- Each chunk includes:
  - The section content
  - The document title (from # heading)  
  - The section name (from ## heading)
  - related_concepts extracted from [[...]] links in ## Related Concepts
  - status extracted from ## Metadata section
  - All existing metadata (page_type, labels, ancestor_titles, source_url, space)
- Minimum chunk size: 50 tokens (skip empty sections)
- Maximum chunk size: 800 tokens (split large sections at paragraph boundaries)
- Prepend document title + section name to chunk content for embedding:
  "[Title] > [Section]: [content]"

### 3. Enhanced Graph Enricher (graph_enricher.py)

Extend the existing ancestor_titles GraphRAG with OKF semantic links:

class EnhancedGraphEnricher:
  - extract_related_concepts(okf_content) → parse [[ConceptName]] from 
    ## Related Concepts section using regex
  - resolve_concepts(related_concepts, all_pages) → find actual page IDs 
    for concept names (fuzzy match on title)
  - build_graph_context(ancestor_titles, related_concepts) → 
    returns a string: "Hierarchy: A > B > C | Related: X, Y, Z"
    This gets stored as graph_context field and embedded alongside content

New pgvector schema additions:
- related_concepts: list[str]  ← OKF semantic links
- graph_context: str           ← Combined hierarchy + semantic links
- okf_converted: bool          ← Flag for converted pages
- okf_file_path: str           ← Path to local OKF file

